Metadata (titles, dates, numbers, links) taken from WIPO Lex, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/, retrieved 30 October 2026. Source: World Intellectual Property Organization. WIPO content is published under CC BY 4.0 (https://www.wipo.int/web/terms-of-use); only facts are copied, with no descriptive text. Open facts about the legal system come from Wikidata, https://www.wikidata.org/ (CC0 1.0).

No law text is included. No official online source for Guinea-Bissau's laws was found, and its copyright code (Decree-Law No. 46 980 of 27 April 1966, extended to the territory by Decree 679/71) has no clause excluding laws from protection, so no third-party copy of a constitution or statute is used.

